<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#f6f3e9"><title>Ritual courts · YUGA map fieldbook</title><style>FIELD_STYLE</style></head>
<body><header><div class="bar"><a href="../" class="brand" aria-label="Yuga production dashboard">YUGA</a><span class="slash">/</span><a href="#top">Cartography</a><nav aria-label="Contents"><a href="#courts">Site plans</a><a href="#setup">Setup</a><a href="#flight">Flight &amp; casts</a><a href="#sources">Field notes</a></nav></div></header>
<main id="top"><div class="introduction"><div><p class="section-id">EMBER RITE &nbsp; / &nbsp; LEVEL DESIGN</p><h1>The ritual courts</h1><p class="dek">Walk all eight sites. Find the second hiding place at an entrance, then follow an arrow, a returning chakra or a flying hero above the floor.</p><a class="top-link" href="#courts">Explore the floorplans <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><figure class="lead-art"><img alt="Mandala Rift concept painting, with a stepped water court, a pillared temple and a riverside market" src="FIELD_ART"><figcaption>Mandala Rift <span>District concept study</span></figcaption></figure></div>
<section id="courts"><div class="chapter"><p class="section-id">01 &nbsp; / &nbsp; ARCHITECTURE</p><h2>At the threshold</h2><p>Choose an approach. Each numbered circle marks a position where a different solid hides the whole body from the selected ground observer. The open diamond marks where that hero can step out and see the observer.</p></div>
<div class="selectors"><label>District<select id="district"></select></label><label>Ritual court<select id="court"></select></label><label>Approach<select id="door"></select></label></div>
<div class="folio"><section class="drawing"><div class="drawing-head"><h3 id="sheet-title"></h3><span id="floor-label"></span></div><svg id="plan" viewBox="0 0 560 460" role="img" aria-label="North-up site plan with collision solids, two hiding positions, exposed peeks and goal rings"></svg><div class="key"><span><i class="hide"></i>Hide</span><span><i class="peek"></i>Peek</span><span><i class="threat"></i>Observer</span><span><i class="actor"></i>Your position</span></div></section>
<aside class="paper"><h3 id="entry-title"></h3><p id="entry-figures" class="figures"></p><div id="pockets"></div><label id="face-label">Observation direction<select id="face"><option value="approach">From the entrance</option><option value="reverse">From the ritual court</option></select></label>
<div class="walking"><button id="walk" type="button">Walk this entrance</button><p id="walk-info" role="status" aria-live="polite">Start at the observer and try both shelters.</p><div class="directions" role="group" aria-label="Walk on the plan"><button data-step="north" aria-label="Move north">↑</button><button data-step="west" aria-label="Move west">←</button><button data-step="south" aria-label="Move south">↓</button><button data-step="east" aria-label="Move east">→</button></div></div></aside></div><p class="caption">Outer dashed ring: 4.5 m apron. Inner ring: 3 m kindle disk. Art landmarks outside the room are omitted. Movement uses the original ground rehearsal collision solver.</p></section>
<section id="setup"><div class="chapter"><p class="section-id">02 &nbsp; / &nbsp; PREPARATION</p><h2>Before the curtain lifts</h2><p>Each team has 20 seconds to walk its side, take a ladder or wait at a curtain. All four lofts are reachable. The routes below start their clocks when the curtains open.</p></div><div class="folio"><section class="drawing"><div class="drawing-head"><h3>Mandala Rift</h3><span>Preparation floor and four lofts</span></div>STAGING_PLATE</section><aside class="paper"><h3>First arrival</h3><p class="figures">Unopposed travel time to the site centre, in seconds.</p><table class="opening"><thead><tr><th>Duty · site</th><th>Spawn, dry</th><th>Prepared, dry</th><th>Prepared, fold allowed</th></tr></thead><tbody>FIELD_OPENING</tbody></table><p class="figures">Spice Loft and Water Loft rise 2.4 m. Cloth Loft and Scale Loft rise 3.2 m. A forward loft opens a new angle and costs time compared with waiting on the floor at the barrier.</p><a href="./mandala-staging.svg">Open staging drawing ↗</a></aside></div></section>
<section id="flight"><div class="chapter"><p class="section-id">03 &nbsp; / &nbsp; VERTICAL MOVEMENT</p><h2>What clears the stone?</h2><p>Read the same fixed-tick cast from the side and from above. A red cross marks the final sample. The chart begins at the first recorded frame and keeps repeated positions during wind-up.</p></div>
<div class="selectors single"><label>Recorded play<select id="trace"></select></label></div><div class="folio"><section class="drawing"><div class="drawing-head"><h3>Elevation section</h3><span>Metres above district datum</span></div><svg id="elevation" viewBox="0 0 560 255" role="img" aria-label="Elevation against elapsed time for the selected play"></svg><div class="drawing-head small"><h3>Plan trace</h3><span>North up · local extent</span></div><svg id="trace-plan" viewBox="0 0 560 150" role="img" aria-label="Horizontal projection of the same trace"></svg></section><aside class="paper"><p class="section-id" id="trace-kind"></p><h3 id="trace-title"></h3><p class="figures" id="trace-result"></p><div class="replay"><label for="scrub">Replay time <output id="playhead" for="scrub"></output></label><input id="scrub" type="range" min="0" step="1" value="0"><button id="play-trace" type="button">Play trace</button></div><ol id="events"></ol></aside></div></section>
<section id="sources"><div class="chapter"><p class="section-id">04 &nbsp; / &nbsp; FIELD NOTES</p><h2>At the design table</h2><p>Measured art heights, proposed competitive hulls, opening clocks and two-team encounter scripts are available with their source data.</p></div>
